Wait, maybe Polka should be the one doing that role after all?

2434
01:59:12,110 --> 01:59:16,030
Because — okay, Ponpon, please!

2435
01:59:16,030 --> 01:59:18,110
Huh, wait, I can't grab it — it's all going past me!

2436
01:59:18,110 --> 01:59:20,770
More, more, give me more!

2437
01:59:20,770 --> 01:59:24,010
Can't get it, can't get it!

2438
01:59:24,010 --> 01:59:27,130
Keep pressing, keep pressing!

2439
01:59:27,130 --> 01:59:29,810
Got the circle — wait, not a circle — got the circle, nice!

2440
01:59:29,810 --> 01:59:33,170
I want the square, the square — I'll use the square as a weight.

2441
01:59:33,170 --> 01:59:36,370
Each time you only get as many as you grabbed —

2442
01:59:36,370 --> 01:59:41,110
the shape keeps falling apart.

2443
01:59:41,110 --> 01:59:43,310
In one go... hmm? What do you call it?

2444
01:59:43,310 --> 01:59:44,710
Ughhhhh!

2445
01:59:44,710 --> 01:59:46,430
Hahhhhhh!

2446
01:59:46,430 --> 01:59:49,430
It has to be done in one go.

2447
01:59:49,430 --> 01:59:50,330
Huh?

2448
01:59:50,330 --> 01:59:52,970
I can only grab the round ones though.

2449
01:59:52,970 --> 01:59:53,730
Yeah.

2450
01:59:53,730 --> 01:59:57,030
And if you fire the next one, that one probably breaks.

2451
01:59:57,030 --> 01:59:58,030
See?

2452
01:59:58,030 --> 02:00:01,510
So that won't work.

2453
02:00:01,550 --> 02:00:04,120
Okay, so then...

2454
02:00:04,120 --> 02:00:06,260
choose between the square or the circle.

2455
02:00:06,260 --> 02:00:08,380
That one probably...

2456
02:00:08,380 --> 02:00:09,980
there's a target,

2457
02:00:09,980 --> 02:00:12,020
so you'll need to shoot through it in the end.

2458
02:00:12,020 --> 02:00:14,720
Anyway, I want to head over to Ponpon's side first.

2459
02:00:14,720 --> 02:00:15,100
Yeah.

2460
02:00:15,100 --> 02:00:18,460
Hah!

2461
02:00:18,460 --> 02:00:19,060
Got away!

2462
02:00:19,060 --> 02:00:22,570
Nice.

2463
02:00:22,570 --> 02:00:27,000
So Ponpon, over there —

2464
02:00:27,000 --> 02:00:28,600
on Ponpon's side,

2465
02:00:28,600 --> 02:00:30,840
there's a passage going through to the white target.

2466
02:00:30,840 --> 02:00:31,980
Can't reach it?

2467
02:00:31,980 --> 02:00:36,210
Ahhhhh...

2468
02:00:36,210 --> 02:00:37,800
Light blue.

2469
02:00:37,800 --> 02:00:40,200
Where does this go?

2470
02:00:40,200 --> 02:00:42,760
It's right above Ponpon's head.

2471
02:00:42,760 --> 02:00:44,200
Oh, there it is, there it is!

2472
02:00:44,200 --> 02:00:44,960
Hey!

2473
02:00:44,960 --> 02:00:47,080
Yeah, yeah, with that —

2474
02:00:47,080 --> 02:00:48,840
put it there.

2475
02:00:48,840 --> 02:00:49,280
Thanks!

2476
02:00:49,280 --> 02:00:51,480
And this one's the anti- one,

2477
02:00:51,480 --> 02:00:57,800
and then from there, probably

2478
02:00:57,800 --> 02:01:01,370
through the hole...

2479
02:01:01,370 --> 02:01:06,550
Wait, is this not Ponpon's?

2480
02:01:06,550 --> 02:01:10,070
How do we...?

2481
02:01:10,070 --> 02:01:13,510
Hmm...

2482
02:01:13,510 --> 02:01:21,150
Hmm, so I pick up one of the shields? But now I can't pick this up anymore.

2483
02:01:23,610 --> 02:01:28,810
Okay, so... what am I supposed to do next?

2484
02:01:28,810 --> 02:01:31,810
Now I'm in front of the shield.

2485
02:01:31,810 --> 02:01:35,330
How do I proceed from here...

2486
02:01:35,330 --> 02:01:39,900
Umm...

2487
02:01:39,900 --> 02:01:42,240
Can I go over this way for a sec?

2488
02:01:42,240 --> 02:01:43,840
Oh, I get shot if I go that way?

2489
02:01:43,840 --> 02:01:47,540
I was wondering how far I'd get before getting shot.

2490
02:01:47,540 --> 02:01:49,320
Do I get shot here?

2491
02:01:49,320 --> 02:01:54,160
How do I reach the goal?

2492
02:01:54,160 --> 02:01:59,260
Running through is definitely impossible. No way.

2493
02:01:59,260 --> 02:02:06,020
Should I try it? Try running through?

2494
02:02:06,020 --> 02:02:11,820
Yeah, that's the thing — it's gone now.

2495
02:02:11,820 --> 02:02:16,020
So I absolutely can't let it go off course.

2496
02:02:16,260 --> 02:02:20,730
Wait, now I can't go back either.

2497
02:02:20,730 --> 02:02:23,870
How do I do this?

2498
02:02:23,870 --> 02:02:27,730
I can't grab the turret. Can't grab it — it's not close enough.

2499
02:02:27,730 --> 02:02:32,620
Huh? Oh— wait, what?

2500
02:02:32,620 --> 02:02:35,060
The turret...

2501
02:02:35,060 --> 02:02:40,220
Wait, if I line it up here and shoot it through here—

2502
02:02:40,220 --> 02:02:41,980
and then press E—

2503
02:02:41,980 --> 02:02:44,930
Wait, what just happened?

2504
02:02:44,930 --> 02:02:46,730
What are you doing?!

2505
02:02:46,730 --> 02:02:48,730
I thought maybe I could take it down with this, but...

2506
02:02:48,730 --> 02:02:49,680
Oh, that's true!

2507
02:02:49,680 --> 02:02:51,530
Big brain!

2508
02:02:51,530 --> 02:02:55,720
Just a little more...

2509
02:02:55,720 --> 02:02:56,720
It didn't go down?!

2510
02:02:56,720 --> 02:02:57,720
It didn't go down?!

2511
02:02:57,720 --> 02:03:04,960
It didn't go down...

2512
02:03:04,960 --> 02:03:06,960
Okay, let's just run.

2513
02:03:06,960 --> 02:03:07,950
Run?

2514
02:03:07,950 --> 02:03:10,760
No, that's definitely wrong — I was already getting shot.

2515
02:03:11,560 --> 02:03:15,560
Look, if I just randomly bounce the shot around, it seems like it might work?

2516
02:03:15,560 --> 02:03:17,360
No good, but it's hitting...

2517
02:03:17,360 --> 02:03:19,160
Oh! It worked! It worked! It's working! Let's go! Let's go!

2518
02:03:19,160 --> 02:03:20,160
Wait, seriously?

2519
02:03:20,160 --> 02:03:21,160
It CAN be taken down?!

2520
02:03:21,160 --> 02:03:22,960
That felt amazing!

2521
02:03:22,960 --> 02:03:24,760
So it CAN be defeated!

2522
02:03:24,760 --> 02:03:28,560
You guys, your feet are way too weak!

2523
02:03:28,560 --> 02:03:29,560
Incredible!

2524
02:03:29,560 --> 02:03:32,560
Seriously? That method...

2525
02:03:32,560 --> 02:03:34,560
THAT was the way?!

2526
02:03:34,560 --> 02:03:36,560
For real? It actually works!

2527
02:03:36,560 --> 02:03:39,360
How about that~

2528
02:03:39,360 --> 02:03:42,480
Man, this really breaks you out of rigid thinking.

2529
02:03:42,480 --> 02:03:43,680
Mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

2530
02:03:43,680 --> 02:03:48,490
Ohhh, I see, I see~

2531
02:03:48,490 --> 02:03:50,090
Ah, that was fun.

2532
02:03:50,090 --> 02:03:53,330
Yeah, this kind of thinking...

2533
02:03:53,330 --> 02:03:55,490
...just went out the window.

2534
02:03:55,490 --> 02:03:58,090
I see, I see.

2535
02:03:58,090 --> 02:03:59,290
Oh!

2536
02:03:59,290 --> 02:04:01,370
Huh, what? What is it?

2537
02:04:01,370 --> 02:04:03,530
Oh, did someone come back?

2538
02:04:03,530 --> 02:04:06,330
Wait, did someone just say good evening?

2539
02:04:06,330 --> 02:04:09,940
You know, whenever the stage changes, something like this always happens.

2540
02:04:09,940 --> 02:04:13,230
Should I just randomly shoot and reach the goal again?

2541
02:04:13,230 --> 02:04:16,530
That's what I'm thinking, anyway.

2542
02:04:16,530 --> 02:04:18,530
Hmm? Not this way.

2543
02:04:18,530 --> 02:04:20,630
But if it's just sitting over here normally, then...

2544
02:04:20,630 --> 02:04:22,430
What the heck?

2545
02:04:22,430 --> 02:04:26,330
So this time, there's nothing this time?!

2546
02:04:26,330 --> 02:04:28,230
But this is actually a really nice spot.

2547
02:04:28,230 --> 02:04:30,230
Hmm, what? There are bullets but I can't shoot them.

2548
02:04:30,230 --> 02:04:33,830
The object disintegrates... the piston stops.

2549
02:04:33,830 --> 02:04:38,750
So this means I can't go up. I can't go up.

2550
02:04:38,750 --> 02:04:42,810
Solve the mystery — come on, what is this?

2551
02:04:42,810 --> 02:04:46,550
What is this? What is this? What IS this?

2552
02:04:46,550 --> 02:04:49,270
What on earth is this?

2553
02:04:49,270 --> 02:04:53,650
Can I put something in here?

2554
02:04:53,650 --> 02:04:57,810
Will it work if there's air?

2555
02:04:57,970 --> 02:05:02,950
I want to place the bullet here, but it's starting to feel like one of those wire puzzles.

2556
02:05:02,950 --> 02:05:04,830
What even is this.

2557
02:05:04,830 --> 02:05:07,550
What does "the piston stops" mean?

2558
02:05:07,550 --> 02:05:10,930
Do I place it here?

2559
02:05:10,930 --> 02:05:12,810
The object disintegrates.

2560
02:05:12,810 --> 02:05:17,120
How do I pick this up?

2561
02:05:17,120 --> 02:05:18,800
Pulverized.

2562
02:05:18,800 --> 02:05:19,800
Well, it's impossible anyway.

2563
02:05:19,800 --> 02:05:22,740
Wait, is there a white wall?

2564
02:05:22,740 --> 02:05:24,520
Oh, there's a wall.

2565
02:05:24,520 --> 02:05:26,520
Can I make one? Huh?

2566
02:05:26,520 --> 02:05:28,520
How do you get the ball

2567
02:05:28,520 --> 02:05:34,480
to shoot through from there?

2568
02:05:34,480 --> 02:05:37,280
Like this, like this!

2569
02:05:37,280 --> 02:05:43,440
How do you even get it in there?

2570
02:05:43,440 --> 02:05:46,240
Will it fit at that height?

2571
02:05:46,240 --> 02:05:49,040
It fell down.

2572
02:05:49,040 --> 02:05:51,840
Looks like it might fit...

2573
02:05:51,840 --> 02:05:53,640
Oh, the belly catches it?

2574
02:05:53,640 --> 02:05:54,640
Here you go!

2575
02:05:55,440 --> 02:05:56,460
Oh, it worked!

2576
02:05:56,460 --> 02:05:58,640
I did it!

2577
02:05:58,640 --> 02:05:59,940
Whoa, yeah!

2578
02:05:59,940 --> 02:06:01,840
Oh, it opened — the entry hole opened!

2579
02:06:01,840 --> 02:06:05,040
Ooh, amazing! I see, I see!

2580
02:06:05,040 --> 02:06:08,640
So there was a white wall on the wall.

2581
02:06:08,640 --> 02:06:13,040
The ball just keeps firing forever... Again, same kind of thing...

2582
02:06:13,040 --> 02:06:15,820
Oh, again.

2583
02:06:15,820 --> 02:06:16,920
Not yet!

2584
02:06:16,920 --> 02:06:18,520
Find the ball!

2585
02:06:18,520 --> 02:06:20,420
Ball catch time, po-po!

2586
02:06:20,420 --> 02:06:21,720
What?! It's po-po!

2587
02:06:21,720 --> 02:06:32,450
Po-po, when it comes to ball catching, it's po-po! Where is the ball catch spot? Somewhere around here? It's flying over!  Where's today's ball catch location?

2588
02:06:32,450 --> 02:06:42,290
I think it might connect somehow. Up there. Where am I even going to land?

2589
02:06:42,630 --> 02:06:48,370
But I kind of have a feeling it might build a shield or something...

2590
02:06:48,370 --> 02:06:51,510
Wait, there's something here.

2591
02:06:51,510 --> 02:06:53,990
Offline.

2592
02:06:53,990 --> 02:06:57,980
What do you mean, offline?

2593
02:06:57,980 --> 02:07:02,380
It's building a shield up top!

2594
02:07:02,380 --> 02:07:03,500
Bang!

2595
02:07:03,500 --> 02:07:04,700
Boom!

2596
02:07:04,700 --> 02:07:07,720
Wait, if it's like this...

2597
02:07:07,720 --> 02:07:12,520
But if it's like this, I can catch the ball, but then it moves back over there again.

2598
02:07:12,520 --> 02:07:15,580
Oh, I said catch, but it's actually a boost.

2599
02:07:15,580 --> 02:07:18,660
There's a yellow one there — isn't that the spot?

2600
02:07:18,660 --> 02:07:20,620
Can't you connect that to somewhere? Po-po.

2601
02:07:20,620 --> 02:07:23,690
It's moving too fast, this is impossible.

2602
02:07:23,690 --> 02:07:27,320
The ball, that spot and...

2603
02:07:27,320 --> 02:07:30,220
How do you dodge it?

2604
02:07:30,220 --> 02:07:34,120
Can't I connect this here and here?

2605
02:07:35,420 --> 02:07:39,720
Po-po, can you connect here and here?

2606
02:07:39,720 --> 02:07:43,660
Here and...

2607
02:07:43,660 --> 02:07:44,760
Where is it?

2608
02:07:44,760 --> 02:07:48,960
Oh, but from here I can't fire the beam.

2609
02:07:48,960 --> 02:07:53,360
Ugh, wait — then where is it supposed to go?

2610
02:07:53,360 --> 02:07:56,860
Where do I connect?

2611
02:07:56,860 --> 02:08:01,240
Hmm, but it'll break, that's true.

2612
02:08:01,240 --> 02:08:08,480
Hmm... I feel like it's supposed to bounce somehow.

2613
02:08:08,480 --> 02:08:14,000
Offline? Well, offline is fine I guess.

2614
02:08:14,000 --> 02:08:19,640
Sorry, I accidentally broke the thing Luna set up. Yeah yeah yeah yeah.

2615
02:08:19,640 --> 02:08:25,830
Okay so this is red — thank you! So using this...

2616
02:08:26,270 --> 02:08:28,730
Is this the part where I put it online?

2617
02:08:28,730 --> 02:08:30,550
Ehh?

2618
02:08:30,550 --> 02:08:37,780
I feel like something should happen from here...

2619
02:08:37,780 --> 02:08:41,480
Can't I remove this shield?

2620
02:08:41,480 --> 02:08:46,220
Earlier when I switched it online or offline, it disappeared, right?

2621
02:08:46,220 --> 02:08:47,200
That's not what I mean.

2622
02:08:47,200 --> 02:08:48,500
Huh? It disappeared?

2623
02:08:48,500 --> 02:08:49,100
Wait, what?

2624
02:08:49,100 --> 02:08:50,100
Yeah.

2625
02:08:50,100 --> 02:08:55,140
Huh?

2626
02:08:55,140 --> 02:08:58,760
It's gone.

2627
02:08:58,760 --> 02:09:00,480
Oh.

2628
02:09:00,480 --> 02:09:07,800
No wait — the one above po-po can be cut, but this thin shield here can't be removed, right?

2629
02:09:07,800 --> 02:09:15,240
Ohhh this one! I connected this and here!

2630
02:09:15,240 --> 02:09:22,340
Oh wait, what about here? Yeah, I was just looking over there thinking there might be something.

2631
02:09:22,340 --> 02:09:27,580
So what does that mean? Yeah, exactly...

2632
02:09:28,660 --> 02:09:32,460
Hmm...

2633
02:09:32,460 --> 02:09:37,230
Hmm...

2634
02:09:37,230 --> 02:09:40,060
That's terrible!

2635
02:09:40,060 --> 02:09:44,790
Aww, red!

2636
02:09:44,790 --> 02:09:52,760
Wait, it seriously can't reach?

2637
02:09:52,760 --> 02:10:02,410
Where does the po-po need to connect to?

2638
02:10:02,410 --> 02:10:04,210
Put the po-po right in front of it — yes!

2639
02:10:04,210 --> 02:10:07,010
If I can't connect them, then... here and here?

2640
02:10:07,010 --> 02:10:09,810
Oh, right, yeah.

2641
02:10:09,810 --> 02:10:12,610
Or here?

2642
02:10:12,610 --> 02:10:13,490
Here?

2643
02:10:13,490 --> 02:10:18,410
Wait, one ball got swallowed up somewhere, but I don't know where it came out.

2644
02:10:18,410 --> 02:10:20,410
Getting swallowed is the right move.

2645
02:10:20,410 --> 02:10:22,850
It went over there.

2646
02:10:22,850 --> 02:10:26,410
Which means...

2647
02:10:26,410 --> 02:10:29,410
It just went somewhere I can't reach.

2648
02:10:29,410 --> 02:10:33,410
I don't think you can catch it here... that's not a thing, right?

2649
02:10:33,410 --> 02:10:37,210
It went somewhere I can't get to.

2650
02:10:37,210 --> 02:10:42,010
Here...

2651
02:10:42,010 --> 02:10:45,760
Huh? Wait.

2652
02:10:45,760 --> 02:10:48,560
Ugh, I can't erase the red one.

2653
02:10:48,560 --> 02:10:52,160
Umm...

2654
02:10:52,160 --> 02:10:54,160
Hm? What's this?

2655
02:10:54,160 --> 02:10:55,960
Ah, it went somewhere.

2656
02:10:57,760 --> 02:11:00,760
Does the blue car do this?

2657
02:11:00,760 --> 02:11:03,560
But that's different, right?

2658
02:11:03,560 --> 02:11:06,560
I need to make a shield.

2659
02:11:06,560 --> 02:11:08,160
Right.

2660
02:11:08,160 --> 02:11:11,960
The shield — guard once,

2661
02:11:11,960 --> 02:11:14,760
and then after that...

2662
02:11:14,760 --> 02:11:20,250
Do it here first? What do we do?

2663
02:11:20,250 --> 02:11:24,830
What should I do with this?

2664
02:11:24,830 --> 02:11:31,830
Well, honestly, if the catch is here, if it's not, Polka can come back this way.

2665
02:11:31,830 --> 02:11:36,800
The bouncing is probably on that side.

2666
02:11:36,800 --> 02:11:38,540
So it is that side?

2667
02:11:38,540 --> 02:11:39,400
Yeah.

2668
02:11:39,400 --> 02:11:40,290
It's big.

2669
02:11:40,290 --> 02:11:42,000
Hmm.

2670
02:11:42,000 --> 02:11:44,000
I think it's just too far away.

2671
02:11:44,000 --> 02:11:45,800
Even if it fits perfectly.

2672
02:11:45,800 --> 02:11:53,080
I think it might be a little too far.

2673
02:11:53,080 --> 02:12:01,680
Catch it diagonally—

2674
02:12:01,680 --> 02:12:04,260
From the ceiling—

2675
02:12:04,260 --> 02:12:06,340
Diagonally.

2676
02:12:06,340 --> 02:12:07,200
Diagonally.

2677
02:12:07,200 --> 02:12:13,730
Diagonally.

2678
02:12:13,730 --> 02:12:18,930
But how do I connect this side and that side?

2679
02:12:18,930 --> 02:12:29,260
Earlier I managed to shoot it diagonally.

2680
02:12:29,260 --> 02:12:31,280
Did I shoot it diagonally earlier?

2681
02:12:31,280 --> 02:12:33,630
Yeah, it was going diagonally somehow.

2682
02:12:33,630 --> 02:12:34,880
How did you do it?

2683
02:12:34,880 --> 02:12:37,200
How did I do that?

2684
02:12:37,200 --> 02:12:39,660
Diagonally, like this?

2685
02:12:39,660 --> 02:12:42,160
Ah, no, not that — what is that? Scary.

2686
02:12:42,160 --> 02:12:45,870
That's new.

2687
02:12:45,870 --> 02:12:47,320
This doesn't work.

2688
02:12:47,320 --> 02:12:50,040
But the shield isn't coming out.

2689
02:12:50,040 --> 02:12:50,930
Huh, like this?

2690
02:12:50,930 --> 02:12:53,500
It seems like I need to do something with this, but what?

2691
02:12:53,500 --> 02:12:54,000
Oh!

2692
02:12:54,000 --> 02:12:55,000
Climb?

2693
02:12:55,000 --> 02:12:56,800
Oh!

2694
02:12:56,800 --> 02:12:58,680
Wait, Popo!

2695
02:12:58,680 --> 02:13:01,680
Popo, connect the yellow spots here and here,

2696
02:13:01,680 --> 02:13:06,280
here and here.

2697
02:13:06,280 --> 02:13:13,300
From here, the belly—

2698
02:13:13,300 --> 02:13:15,300
Like this, and like this.

2699
02:13:15,300 --> 02:13:18,140
Oh, Popo?

2700
02:13:18,140 --> 02:13:19,300
What?

2701
02:13:19,300 --> 02:13:21,580
- The blue one here... - Where? Oh, here!

2702
02:13:21,580 --> 02:13:22,880
- Here. - Yes, yes, yes!

2703
02:13:22,880 --> 02:13:25,040
- Here and on top of this one— - Got it!

2704
02:13:25,040 --> 02:13:29,480
OK, like this, and this, and this.

2705
02:13:29,480 --> 02:13:31,150
Hm?

2706
02:13:31,150 --> 02:13:33,300
Oh! Nice!

2707
02:13:33,300 --> 02:13:34,740
Huh? Blue, where'd it go?

2708
02:13:34,740 --> 02:13:37,250
Maybe Luna grabs it?

2709
02:13:37,250 --> 02:13:41,050
- Polka, even if you move here... don't move. - The ball... I found the ball!

2710
02:13:41,050 --> 02:13:42,670
Nice!

2711
02:13:42,670 --> 02:13:47,150
- The ball... found it! - Found the ball! Yay!

2712
02:13:47,150 --> 02:13:54,760
This is really bad — oh wait, the game's about to crash — Aah! Luna!

2713
02:13:54,760 --> 02:14:03,400
Why is it crashing here?! The game just crashed suddenly. It's okay, Luna's still— wait, is Luna moving?

2714
02:14:03,400 --> 02:14:13,720
Oh, that's the in-game character. But if Luna comes back... oh... wait... hold on, there's an invite...

2715
02:14:13,720 --> 02:14:15,900
I see, I must accept the invite.

2716
02:14:15,900 --> 02:14:17,420
Why — wait — rejoining.

2717
02:14:17,420 --> 02:14:19,840
Can you rejoin?

2718
02:14:19,840 --> 02:14:22,480
I wonder if there's a way to regroup.

2719
02:14:22,480 --> 02:14:26,100
Can I rejoin?

2720
02:14:26,100 --> 02:14:30,060
Wait, wait, wait — hey, are you kidding me?!

2721
02:14:30,060 --> 02:14:32,020
The track noise is super loud, huh.

2722
02:14:32,020 --> 02:14:33,520
Right? It's really loud.

2723
02:14:33,520 --> 02:14:37,640
The max volume right now is—

2724
02:14:37,640 --> 02:14:40,740
Wait, can we actually rejoin each other in co-op?

2725
02:14:40,740 --> 02:14:44,540
If we can't merge, Polka will go back and re-invite you.

2726
02:14:44,540 --> 02:14:48,540
Hmm, wait— Standard Co-op Mode? Challenge Co-op Mode?

2727
02:14:48,540 --> 02:14:50,540
It was Standard Co-op Mode.

2728
02:14:50,540 --> 02:14:53,220
Did it end up on the selection screen?

2729
02:14:53,220 --> 02:14:56,140
Yeah, a bunch of people's names just popped up.

2730
02:14:56,140 --> 02:15:00,140
Not here.

2731
02:15:00,140 --> 02:15:03,210
This isn't the right place, is it?

2732
02:15:03,210 --> 02:15:06,080
Okay, Polka's going back.

2733
02:15:06,080 --> 02:15:08,010
I'll re-invite you.

2734
02:15:08,010 --> 02:15:12,210
Yeah, you might have to re-invite me, otherwise it won't work.

2735
02:15:12,210 --> 02:15:15,070
Where is this from... Utata's friend list got spotted by Miita.

2736
02:15:15,070 --> 02:15:18,810
Well, friend lists — show off your friends to everyone!

2737
02:15:18,810 --> 02:15:23,610
"Look how many friends I have!" — Friend list. Wait, can we merge here?

2738
02:15:23,610 --> 02:15:26,510
I think we can merge.

2739
02:15:26,510 --> 02:15:30,810
I'm just wondering from where. "Searching for an online partner..."

2740
02:15:30,810 --> 02:15:34,110
Searching now — how's it looking?

2741
02:15:34,110 --> 02:15:40,530
Oh! An invite came! Thank goodness, truly, truly thank goodness.

2742
02:15:40,530 --> 02:15:43,200
That was close, that was close!

2743
02:15:43,200 --> 02:15:49,180
Can we get in? But I wonder where we'll start from...

2744
02:15:49,180 --> 02:15:52,880
Hey, where are you, babe?

2745
02:15:52,880 --> 02:16:02,200
No way— what?! AAAAAAH! It's back to the very beginning! It's the default, but this is where 3-4 ended!

2746
02:16:02,200 --> 02:16:07,200
Wait, where— what— huh?

2747
02:16:07,200 --> 02:16:15,100
So wait, does this mean we're starting from 3-8? Is that what this is?

2748
02:16:15,100 --> 02:16:17,400
Please let that be right.

2749
02:16:17,400 --> 02:16:22,450
If we're starting from 3-8, that's not so bad, right?

2750
02:16:22,450 --> 02:16:24,590
Yeah.

2751
02:16:24,590 --> 02:16:28,500
Alright!

2752
02:16:28,500 --> 02:16:30,400
Wait, how far did Korona get?

2753
02:16:30,400 --> 02:16:33,400
Huh? Something went back. Why?

2754
02:16:33,400 --> 02:16:34,200
No way.

2755
02:16:34,200 --> 02:16:35,710
Something went back.

2756
02:16:35,710 --> 02:16:43,450
But 3-8 is showing as cleared.

2757
02:16:43,450 --> 02:16:43,750
Nice.

2758
02:16:43,750 --> 02:16:46,940
Okay, good.

2759
02:16:46,940 --> 02:16:48,740
Alright, can you make it, Pol?

2760
02:16:48,740 --> 02:16:51,940
She's here!

2761
02:16:51,940 --> 02:16:53,540
I feel like it's showing 8.

2762
02:16:53,540 --> 02:16:57,040
Is 8 cleared? It's showing 8.

2763
02:16:57,040 --> 02:16:58,940
Wait, did we do 8 earlier?

2764
02:16:58,940 --> 02:17:01,140
Did we?

2765
02:17:01,140 --> 02:17:03,140
Huh? Did we clear it?

2766
02:17:03,140 --> 02:17:06,720
I feel like we cleared it... wait?

2767
02:17:06,720 --> 02:17:11,440
I don't know — was that 8? Did we do the 8 gimmick first?

2768
02:17:11,440 --> 02:17:12,800
I don't know.

2769
02:17:12,800 --> 02:17:17,420
What number was that earlier? I'm not sure if that was included in 8.

2770
02:17:17,420 --> 02:17:20,800
Ah, wait — no, that WAS 8. That was 8. Nice!

2771
02:17:20,800 --> 02:17:25,960
So that was 8... Ah, we're starting from here again?

2772
02:17:26,960 --> 02:17:30,400
Oh thank goodness. Well, yeah.

2773
02:17:30,400 --> 02:17:34,740
Wait, we're starting from way back here? Hold on, we're doing this from the beginning again?

2774
02:17:34,740 --> 02:17:36,900
Do you remember?

2775
02:17:36,900 --> 02:17:39,400
It'd be better to have Luna do it than us.

2776
02:17:39,400 --> 02:17:42,220
Okay, I'll do it then.

2777
02:17:42,220 --> 02:17:44,320
Here we go.

2778
02:17:44,320 --> 02:17:46,040
Ahaha, already here!

2779
02:17:46,040 --> 02:17:48,280
Get it, get it, get it!

2780
02:17:48,280 --> 02:17:51,240
Get it!

2781
02:17:51,240 --> 02:17:53,040
Why can't I grab it?

2782
02:17:53,040 --> 02:18:08,890
It's a good button, why can't I grab it?

2783
02:18:08,890 --> 02:18:12,490
Got it!

2784
02:18:12,490 --> 02:18:16,090
Okay okay, we might be a little too in sync.

2785
02:18:16,090 --> 02:18:18,090
My throat hurts, I'm gonna have a lozenge.

2786
02:18:18,090 --> 02:18:19,950
Sure thing.

2787
02:18:19,950 --> 02:18:34,280
So how did we do it again just now?

2788
02:18:34,280 --> 02:18:36,260
The thing from before, right?

2789
02:18:36,260 --> 02:18:38,080
Which spots were it?

2790
02:18:38,080 --> 02:18:40,080
Please wait, I'll make it now.

2791
02:18:40,080 --> 02:18:44,080
Ah, I remember — we also have to do the same offline stuff, right?

2792
02:18:46,050 --> 02:18:54,650
Pol, on your side — holes here and here.

2793
02:18:54,650 --> 02:18:56,250
Here?

2794
02:18:56,250 --> 02:18:58,850
Yeah, yeah.

2795
02:18:58,850 --> 02:19:06,830
And then, run.

2796
02:19:06,830 --> 02:19:10,860
And it rolls over.

2797
02:19:10,860 --> 02:19:13,860
And then we collect it.

2798
02:19:13,860 --> 02:19:15,860
Okay, it went!

2799
02:19:15,860 --> 02:19:17,860
Yes! Nice!

2800
02:19:17,860 --> 02:19:21,660
And this is where we got stuck, right? It'll be fine this time.

2801
02:19:21,660 --> 02:19:23,660
Yeah, the ice fell!

2802
02:19:23,660 --> 02:19:25,660
Okay, let's go this way!

2803
02:19:25,660 --> 02:19:27,260
Shizuko...

2804
02:19:27,260 --> 02:19:28,140
Hmm?

2805
02:19:28,140 --> 02:19:29,860
Something again...

2806
02:19:29,860 --> 02:19:32,660
What? Oh, maybe we need to pull the lever together?

2807
02:19:32,660 --> 02:19:34,660
Oh, I see! Okay.

2808
02:19:34,660 --> 02:19:38,790
Ready, go!

2809
02:19:38,790 --> 02:19:41,590
That was easy!

2810
02:19:41,590 --> 02:19:42,590
Timing, timing!

2811
02:19:42,590 --> 02:19:44,390
Huh?

2812
02:19:44,390 --> 02:19:46,190
What?

2813
02:19:46,190 --> 02:19:49,990
There are a lot of walls again.

2814
02:19:49,990 --> 02:19:51,990
There's also something called a bridge.

2815
02:19:51,990 --> 02:19:54,790
This one says 1, it's written right here.

2816
02:19:54,790 --> 02:19:56,590
What?

2817
02:19:56,590 --> 02:19:58,590
1, 1, 1, 1...

2818
02:19:58,590 --> 02:20:00,390
Oh, oh, 1, 1!

2819
02:20:00,390 --> 02:20:03,390
Wait, wait, wait — it's diagonal again!

2820
02:20:03,390 --> 02:20:06,190
There's a lot of stuff here.

2821
02:20:06,190 --> 02:20:08,990
A 1 came! A 1!

2822
02:20:08,990 --> 02:20:12,240
I feel like last time we started from 1.

2823
02:20:12,240 --> 02:20:13,920
Yeah, I think so too.

2824
02:20:13,920 --> 02:20:17,770
Oh, but this is a place we can just walk to normally.

2825
02:20:17,770 --> 02:20:21,140
Probably...

2826
02:20:21,140 --> 02:20:23,440
Oh, something's happening!

2827
02:20:23,440 --> 02:20:24,540
Where is this?

2828
02:20:24,540 --> 02:20:27,120
Probably this beam here.

2829
02:20:27,120 --> 02:20:30,720
We need to do something with the beam.

2830
02:20:30,720 --> 02:20:32,560
Where do we connect it to?

2831
02:20:32,560 --> 02:20:33,980
But connect 1 to 1...

2832
02:20:33,980 --> 02:20:38,320
Oh, with 1... right, so we connect 1 to 1.

2833
02:20:38,320 --> 02:20:42,320
So 1 is here, right? The partner 1?

2834
02:20:42,320 --> 02:20:45,180
And we keep connecting them like that.

2835
02:20:45,180 --> 02:20:49,780
Can we go up? Can we?

2836
02:20:49,780 --> 02:20:56,320
First, let's see if we can get over there.

2837
02:20:56,320 --> 02:21:03,680
I want to get in somewhere first.

2838
02:21:03,680 --> 02:21:07,480
Ponpon says connect 1 to 1.

2839
02:21:09,330 --> 02:21:12,330
Ponpon's throat is in bad shape.

2840
02:21:12,330 --> 02:21:15,130
But she says 1 and 1 connected!

2841
02:21:15,130 --> 02:21:17,930
So what if they connected?

2842
02:21:17,930 --> 02:21:20,730
That beam...

2843
02:21:20,730 --> 02:21:31,230
What does that mean?

2844
02:21:31,230 --> 02:21:33,230
There's one up top too.

2845
02:21:33,230 --> 02:21:38,320
This one's a 2.

2846
02:21:41,020 --> 02:21:46,880
1 goes with 1, 2 goes with 2? Maybe not though.

2847
02:21:46,880 --> 02:21:51,300
If we connect it this way, then... but how do you even get in there?

2848
02:21:51,300 --> 02:21:57,440
Oh, can we go from this side? From the yellow? We can go from yellow — let's go!

2849
02:21:57,440 --> 02:22:01,640
We climbed up, but where do we go? I feel like it's impossible.

2850
02:22:01,640 --> 02:22:05,920
Where do we go from here? From this spot?

2851
02:22:05,920 --> 02:22:10,000
I'm not sure where to go. There's really nowhere obvious.

2852
02:22:10,000 --> 02:22:17,000
There is a diagonal on this side too, I guess.

2853
02:22:17,000 --> 02:22:22,380
Hmm, where do we connect it? Oh, that direction might be...

2854
02:22:22,380 --> 02:22:27,700
Looks like we might be able to go somewhere. That 2 spot.

2855
02:22:27,700 --> 02:22:31,860
Which 2? Hmm, no, that's not it.

2856
02:22:32,160 --> 02:22:39,040
It looked possible because it was on the opposite side. Hmm.

2857
02:22:39,040 --> 02:22:48,560
Hmm. We need one more white wall. In the end we want to extend it to the exit.

2858
02:22:48,560 --> 02:22:55,790
Hmm. Actually, isn't this the spot?

2859
02:22:55,790 --> 02:23:01,060
This is where we want to end up, right? Here?

2860
02:23:01,060 --> 02:23:03,950
But at that angle...

2861
02:23:03,950 --> 02:23:08,390
Wait, can we do it? Can we climb up and then fall down?

2862
02:23:08,390 --> 02:23:12,190
It's hard to judge the distance from over here.

2863
02:23:12,190 --> 02:23:17,790
We'll hit something — some kind of metal thing.

2864
02:23:17,790 --> 02:23:24,100
We'll hit it? Hmm, we can't just crash into it.

2865
02:23:24,100 --> 02:23:28,980
Oh, you're right! There's a barrier there! There's a boundary to this world!

2866
02:23:28,980 --> 02:23:33,310
Right here — how do we get past this?

2867
02:23:33,310 --> 02:23:39,310
We have to find a way to cross this world boundary.

2868
02:23:39,310 --> 02:23:45,450
Oh, we're in the middle! The middle? The middle?

2869
02:23:45,450 --> 02:23:51,010
That's the EXIT over there, right? That's the goal.

2870
02:23:52,310 --> 02:23:54,950
A path that leads here.

2871
02:23:54,950 --> 02:23:57,550
We need a diagonal like this from 1 or 2.

2872
02:23:57,550 --> 02:23:59,310
That steep one won't work.

2873
02:23:59,310 --> 02:24:01,310
It was the same kind of thing from 1 too.

2874
02:24:01,310 --> 02:24:06,160
There's nothing below, right?

2875
02:24:06,160 --> 02:24:17,380
There's something we're missing.

2876
02:24:17,380 --> 02:24:24,540
Another falling thing?

2877
02:24:24,540 --> 02:24:30,900
Have it go diagonal so we fall instead of going up.

2878
02:24:30,900 --> 02:24:35,860
But wait, did we figure that out before?

2879
02:24:35,860 --> 02:24:42,610
Fall onto 1 or 2 and then bounce — like that?

2880
02:24:42,610 --> 02:24:47,430
Oh, is that it? So like this?

2881
02:24:47,430 --> 02:24:52,490
Isn't it like this? Uh, where was the last part? Yeah, yeah, yeah.

2882
02:24:52,490 --> 02:24:54,490
In this case...

2883
02:24:54,490 --> 02:24:58,510
Alright, let's try falling down from here for now.

2884
02:24:58,510 --> 02:25:02,000
Here we go... whoa!

2885
02:25:02,000 --> 02:25:02,710
Whoa!

2886
02:25:02,710 --> 02:25:04,510
Hey! That went way too far!

2887
02:25:04,510 --> 02:25:06,510
That was close!

2888
02:25:06,510 --> 02:25:09,120
We flew too far.

2889
02:25:09,120 --> 02:25:11,110
Even so, it feels like we're so close.

2890
02:25:11,110 --> 02:25:13,110
The idea seems right though.

2891
02:25:13,110 --> 02:25:15,110
It wasn't because we went through 2 that it failed, right?

2892
02:25:15,110 --> 02:25:18,110
Like, if we went through 1, it would actually work?

2893
02:25:19,910 --> 02:25:24,210
Hmm, but the exit is the same...

2894
02:25:24,210 --> 02:25:30,800
1, 2... maybe not?

2895
02:25:30,800 --> 02:25:35,680
If only the current one would become like a vertical... well, not exactly vertical, but

2896
02:25:35,680 --> 02:25:38,680
like a shield, a stopper for us.

2897
02:25:38,680 --> 02:25:42,120
Yeah, but there's nothing like that.

2898
02:25:42,120 --> 02:25:47,120
What? There can't be anything in the way while we're flying, right?

2899
02:25:47,120 --> 02:25:57,290
Hmm... hmm...

2900
02:25:57,290 --> 02:26:01,440
Try falling from this side too. About the same?

2901
02:26:01,440 --> 02:26:16,620
This side — here we go! Whoa! Same! Exactly the same! Yeah, same. We have too much momentum.

2902
02:26:17,000 --> 02:26:21,040
Maybe here... oh wait, you can't press here?

2903
02:26:21,040 --> 02:26:24,410
Wheeee~

2904
02:26:24,410 --> 02:26:30,950
Seriously?

2905
02:26:30,950 --> 02:26:36,950
It won't become a wall.

2906
02:26:36,950 --> 02:26:41,390
Even if we angle it diagonally...

2907
02:26:41,390 --> 02:26:42,950
Why are there 1 and 2?

2908
02:26:42,950 --> 02:26:45,250
Yeah, it's weird that there's a 1 and a 2.

2909
02:26:45,250 --> 02:26:48,710
And I couldn't really tell the difference between 1 and 2.

2910
02:26:48,710 --> 02:26:50,550
They felt the same.

2911
02:26:50,550 --> 02:26:54,550
Yeah, right. The result of barely making it through was the same too.

2912
02:26:54,550 --> 02:26:59,350
Hmm.

2913
02:26:59,350 --> 02:27:02,150
Why are there two of us? Should we go together?

2914
02:27:02,150 --> 02:27:03,950
Huh?

2915
02:27:03,950 --> 02:27:05,950
Ohh.

2916
02:27:05,950 --> 02:27:08,610
Oh, maybe that's it!

2917
02:27:08,610 --> 02:27:13,550
It was simple — two people collide, two people. The idea was simple.

2918
02:27:13,550 --> 02:27:15,350
Totally.

2919
02:27:15,350 --> 02:27:18,120
So? And then?

2920
02:27:18,920 --> 02:27:21,400
So we both fall together?

2921
02:27:21,400 --> 02:27:25,120
Maybe we don't even need to fall? Actually.

2922
02:27:25,120 --> 02:27:25,720
You think?

2923
02:27:25,720 --> 02:27:27,560
We still need to fall though, right?

2924
02:27:27,560 --> 02:27:30,860
Yeah, we need the fall.

2925
02:27:30,860 --> 02:27:34,160
Without the fall, the distance won't work out.

2926
02:27:34,160 --> 02:27:35,920
So Luna has a bit of a tough job then?

2927
02:27:35,920 --> 02:27:37,580
How do we even do this?

2928
02:27:37,580 --> 02:27:39,260
Umm...

2929
02:27:39,260 --> 02:27:41,520
There's no hole.

2930
02:27:41,520 --> 02:27:44,060
The hole...

2931
02:27:44,060 --> 02:27:48,220
Luna would have to instantly make two holes.

2932
02:27:48,220 --> 02:27:50,040
That's impossible...

2933
02:27:50,040 --> 02:27:51,680
We can't fall through the same hole.

2934
02:27:51,680 --> 02:27:53,160
Would that not work?

2935
02:27:53,160 --> 02:27:54,540
Exactly.

2936
02:27:54,540 --> 02:27:55,340
Wait a second.

2937
02:27:55,340 --> 02:27:59,320
And we can't even pass each other here.

2938
02:27:59,320 --> 02:27:59,920
What?

2939
02:27:59,920 --> 02:28:05,790
So you want it on that side.

2940
02:28:05,790 --> 02:28:07,970
In that case, Luna-tan would...

2941
02:28:07,970 --> 02:28:09,550
make the hole for us.

2942
02:28:09,550 --> 02:28:10,330
Thank you!

2943
02:28:10,330 --> 02:28:12,430
Isn't this hard though?

2944
02:28:12,430 --> 02:28:14,370
Like, making them quickly one after another.

2945
02:28:14,370 --> 02:28:16,170
Exactly.

2946
02:28:16,170 --> 02:28:18,170
At the 2 spot.

2947
02:28:18,170 --> 02:28:19,970
Whaaaat!?

2948
02:28:19,970 --> 02:28:21,970
That's difficult.

2949
02:28:21,970 --> 02:28:25,700
What!?

2950
02:28:25,700 --> 02:28:27,750
Probably...

2951
02:28:27,750 --> 02:28:29,750
If even one gets cut off, it's over right then.

2952
02:28:29,750 --> 02:28:31,350
First of all...

2953
02:28:31,350 --> 02:28:33,350
Like, bam bam?

2954
02:28:33,350 --> 02:28:35,350
Bam bam.

2955
02:28:35,350 --> 02:28:37,180
Well, bam bam...

2956
02:28:37,180 --> 02:28:38,950
Bam bam, and

2957
02:28:38,950 --> 02:28:40,950
bam bam while also holding Luna.

2958
02:28:40,950 --> 02:28:42,750
Don't go in.

2959
02:28:42,750 --> 02:28:44,750
Well, well, well, it's fine.

2960
02:28:44,750 --> 02:28:46,380
Ready, go!

2961
02:28:46,380 --> 02:28:48,270
Bam bam bam bam!

2962
02:28:48,270 --> 02:28:50,050
Where's the ruler?

2963
02:28:50,050 --> 02:28:53,950
I couldn't get into the hole

2964
02:28:53,950 --> 02:28:55,550
Sorry about that

2965
02:28:55,550 --> 02:28:57,550
Maybe Polka was a little bad at it

2966
02:28:57,550 --> 02:28:59,550
At making the hole

2967
02:28:59,550 --> 02:29:01,550
Yeah, we were off

2968
02:29:01,550 --> 02:29:03,550
I'm always bad at getting in on time

2969
02:29:03,550 --> 02:29:05,550
It's fine, it's fine

2970
02:29:05,550 --> 02:29:07,550
But wait, did Ponpon make it just now?

2971
02:29:07,550 --> 02:29:09,350
Yeah, I made it!

2972
02:29:09,350 --> 02:29:11,350
Oh really? So we were doing it right?

2973
02:29:11,350 --> 02:29:13,350
I think so

2974
02:29:13,350 --> 02:29:17,150
Well, if Luna messes up next time, let's fall back

2975
02:29:17,150 --> 02:29:21,950
Oh wait, should Polka not come over here first?

2976
02:29:21,950 --> 02:29:24,550
Oh, why did I fall?

2977
02:29:24,550 --> 02:29:26,550
Oh, Pupu, block it!

2978
02:29:26,550 --> 02:29:28,550
Hey!

2979
02:29:28,550 --> 02:29:31,350
And then Pupu—

2980
02:29:31,350 --> 02:29:34,150
Okay, make a hole for me, please

2981
02:29:34,150 --> 02:29:35,950
Okay, making it. Please.

2982
02:29:35,950 --> 02:29:39,550
Okay, there you go, please.

2983
02:29:39,550 --> 02:29:42,340
And then Popo goes first, please.

2984
02:29:42,340 --> 02:29:44,150
Please, please.

2985
02:29:44,150 --> 02:29:48,190
So Luna, is it okay if I make mine and then fall?

2986
02:29:48,190 --> 02:29:51,030
That's how it'll be.

2987
02:29:51,030 --> 02:29:52,030
OK.

2988
02:29:52,030 --> 02:29:56,380
Quick, quick. Can we do it?

2989
02:29:56,380 --> 02:30:00,180
Taking responsibility for yourself.

2990
02:30:00,180 --> 02:30:01,980
Do your best.

2991
02:30:02,780 --> 02:30:04,780
Here we go!

2992
02:30:04,780 --> 02:30:06,580
Let's go!

2993
02:30:06,580 --> 02:30:08,380
Ready, go!

2994
02:30:08,380 --> 02:30:10,380
Polka's fine though!

2995
02:30:10,380 --> 02:30:12,220
We made it!

2996
02:30:12,220 --> 02:30:19,980
That was pure brute force

2997
02:30:19,980 --> 02:30:21,780
Amazing

2998
02:30:21,780 --> 02:30:23,780
If you're too rigid about it

2999
02:30:23,780 --> 02:30:25,780
There's no way you can do something like this

3000
02:30:25,780 --> 02:30:35,820
Yeah yeah yeah, it's fine, two people doing it together — oh right, that's how it works

3001
02:30:35,820 --> 02:30:40,800
Hmm, I thought we failed just now — not at all!

3002
02:30:40,800 --> 02:30:44,320
- That was fun - What are they saying?

3003
02:30:44,320 --> 02:30:48,160
- They seem to be having fun - Blah blah blah blah blah

3004
02:30:48,160 --> 02:30:52,920
- Huh? Oh, there it is, yes yes, going straight to the new stage doing the same thing as before - Scrapped again

3005
02:30:52,920 --> 02:30:56,660
- Got scrapped again - Got scrapped again

3006
02:30:56,660 --> 02:30:59,860
Man, that's amazing

3007
02:30:59,860 --> 02:31:02,060
That was fun

3008
02:31:02,060 --> 02:31:03,760
Oh, with this?

3009
02:31:03,760 --> 02:31:07,870
- I never expected you to make it this far - Bridge building

3010
02:31:07,870 --> 02:31:10,540
We did bridge building, those kinds of people

3011
02:31:10,540 --> 02:31:13,220
What's the next one— oh! Ooh!

3012
02:31:13,220 --> 02:31:15,660
Ooh, there's some kind of path

3013
02:31:15,660 --> 02:31:18,240
Wait, it's showing how many steps we walked

3014
02:31:18,240 --> 02:31:19,920
Yeah, it's been showing that the whole time, actually

3015
02:31:19,920 --> 02:31:21,340
Oh, I didn't know that was there

3016
02:31:21,340 --> 02:31:24,740
Wait, cooperation points: -174, what does that even mean?

3017
02:31:24,740 --> 02:31:27,600
Huh, where does it say that? Oh, here?

3018
02:31:27,600 --> 02:31:29,400
Cooperation points?

3019
02:31:29,400 --> 02:31:32,100
Oh, it shows the number of portals used and stuff

3020
02:31:32,100 --> 02:31:34,120
Wait, all our records are here

3021
02:31:34,120 --> 02:31:35,760
It says "We are watching you"

3022
02:31:35,760 --> 02:31:37,100
We're being exposed

3023
02:31:37,100 --> 02:31:38,720
"We are watching you"

3024
02:31:38,720 --> 02:31:41,460
Hugs: just one, as usual

3025
02:31:41,460 --> 02:31:44,340
That's fine, one hug is still one hug

3026
02:31:44,340 --> 02:31:46,140
Below average

3027
02:31:46,140 --> 02:31:49,540
But we walked almost the same number of steps

3028
02:31:49,540 --> 02:31:50,680
Yeah

3029
02:31:50,680 --> 02:31:51,420
Surprising

3030
02:31:51,420 --> 02:31:52,900
We were wandering around

3031
02:31:52,900 --> 02:31:57,340
Transport panel

3032
02:31:57,340 --> 02:31:59,440
How do you even hug?

3033
02:31:59,440 --> 02:32:02,800
There was some way to do it, right?

3034
02:32:02,800 --> 02:32:04,800
"Not enough hugs"

3035
02:32:04,800 --> 02:32:06,740
"Transport funnel"

3036
02:32:06,740 --> 02:32:07,580
What's a "transport funnel"?

3037
02:32:07,580 --> 02:32:09,740
"Transport"... what? Again...

3038
02:32:09,740 --> 02:32:11,880
Another hard one... do we launch something?

3039
02:32:11,880 --> 02:32:14,640
Oh, this looks fun

3040
02:32:14,640 --> 02:32:16,440
"Launch the funnel"

3041
02:32:16,440 --> 02:32:17,840
"Funnels"

3042
02:32:17,840 --> 02:32:21,420
You mean those things on the back...?

3043
02:32:21,420 --> 02:32:21,860
Yeah.

3044
02:32:21,860 --> 02:32:23,020
Like the funnels on the back of a Gundam?

3045
02:32:23,020 --> 02:32:24,460
Yes, yes, exactly!

3046
02:32:24,460 --> 02:32:28,720
Whoa, there's something here! It's rolling around!

3047
02:32:28,720 --> 02:32:29,720
Whoosh!

3048
02:32:29,720 --> 02:32:30,720
Oh no.

3049
02:32:30,720 --> 02:32:32,720
What is this? It looks like it's about to teleport me.

3050
02:32:32,720 --> 02:32:37,320
Ahahahahahaha!

3051
02:32:37,320 --> 02:32:40,120
Teleporting... teleporting...

3052
02:32:40,120 --> 02:32:47,720
Don't you have to build something or it won't actually teleport you?

3053
02:32:47,720 --> 02:32:50,520
Okay, I'm floating.

3054
02:32:50,520 --> 02:32:54,320
Oh, I floated! Oh, I floated!

3055
02:32:54,320 --> 02:32:56,320
You're being teleported!

3056
02:32:56,320 --> 02:32:59,120
It looks like this connects to somewhere.

3057
02:32:59,120 --> 02:33:03,220
Where does this connect to?

3058
02:33:03,220 --> 02:33:07,640
Can't go back on foot.

3059
02:33:07,640 --> 02:33:09,420
Wait, this connects where?

3060
02:33:09,420 --> 02:33:11,340
Probably here...

3061
02:33:11,340 --> 02:33:13,520
This connects to somewhere.

3062
02:33:13,520 --> 02:33:15,880
Where do I build it?

3063
02:33:15,880 --> 02:33:20,800
There's a transfer station at my feet!

3064
02:33:20,800 --> 02:33:22,740
That's scary, for real.

3065
02:33:22,740 --> 02:33:24,220
Where was it?

3066
02:33:24,220 --> 02:33:26,020
After that...

3067
02:33:26,020 --> 02:33:28,020
Wait, where am I going to fall?

3068
02:33:28,020 --> 02:33:29,020
Oh, there it is — Luna, right here!

3069
02:33:29,020 --> 02:33:30,020
Where?

3070
02:33:30,020 --> 02:33:31,820
Up, directly above.

3071
02:33:31,820 --> 02:33:32,620
Oh, here it is.

3072
02:33:32,620 --> 02:33:33,620
Yep.

3073
02:33:33,620 --> 02:33:38,340
There was something like a button to press earlier.

3074
02:33:38,340 --> 02:33:39,220
The button's here!

3075
02:33:39,220 --> 02:33:42,220
Then the stuff below will come rushing up.

3076
02:33:42,220 --> 02:33:44,220
Oh, the floor appeared!

3077
02:33:44,220 --> 02:33:48,020
Wait, this is the tutorial?!

3078
02:33:48,020 --> 02:33:48,820
Isn't this insane?

3079
02:33:48,820 --> 02:33:50,820
Ahhh!

3080
02:33:50,820 --> 02:33:52,620
Huh?

3081
02:33:52,620 --> 02:33:58,420
Apparently if you nudge the button, the floor disappears.

3082
02:33:58,420 --> 02:34:02,810
Oh no...

3083
02:34:02,810 --> 02:34:04,610
I'm going back.

3084
02:34:04,610 --> 02:34:06,410
Wait, one more time!

3085
02:34:06,410 --> 02:34:10,210
I'm heading back, just wait.

3086
02:34:10,210 --> 02:34:12,210
Wasn't it fine not to go back though?

3087
02:34:12,210 --> 02:34:14,010
Oh, really?

3088
02:34:14,010 --> 02:34:15,810
Can you do this alone?

3089
02:34:15,810 --> 02:34:16,810
Can you not?

3090
02:34:16,810 --> 02:34:18,740
I don't know.

3091
02:34:18,740 --> 02:34:23,610
So Polka comes here and it's like, "Have a safe trip!"

3092
02:34:23,610 --> 02:34:30,480
Okay, spinning around — oh, this is so satisfying to watch.

3093
02:34:30,480 --> 02:34:33,480
So, this connects here and here?

3094
02:34:33,480 --> 02:34:37,900
And then, meow meow meow meow meow meow meow meow!

3095
02:34:37,900 --> 02:34:42,700
If I don't keep pressing this, the floor thing...

3096
02:34:42,700 --> 02:34:45,700
Won't it stay open? Maybe something like that?

3097
02:34:45,700 --> 02:34:49,500
Wait, did Polka mess something up? Is that what happened?

3098
02:34:49,500 --> 02:34:51,300
No?

3099
02:34:51,300 --> 02:34:55,100
Maybe you need to do something with a ball or something?

3100
02:34:55,100 --> 02:34:58,700
Wait, did I mess something up?

3101
02:34:58,700 --> 02:35:00,690
Oh, this?

3102
02:35:00,690 --> 02:35:02,500
Wait, no, that's not it!

3103
02:35:02,500 --> 02:35:07,550
Wait, what just happened? Did you press something?

3104
02:35:07,550 --> 02:35:10,440
No, I didn't press anything, I just fell.

3105
02:35:10,440 --> 02:35:13,240
Wait, does something happen to the ball or something?

3106
02:35:13,240 --> 02:35:16,030
Huh?

3107
02:35:16,030 --> 02:35:17,840
Was there something like that?

3108
02:35:17,840 --> 02:35:19,640
What is it?

3109
02:35:19,640 --> 02:35:26,990
Connect the panels?

3110
02:35:26,990 --> 02:35:32,260
So one person just keeps traveling the whole time?

3111
02:35:32,260 --> 02:35:35,170
What?

3112
02:35:36,980 --> 02:35:37,780
Huh?

3113
02:35:37,780 --> 02:35:40,780
You're just traveling the whole time? Like this?

3114
02:35:40,780 --> 02:35:44,380
Oh wait, no no no, something's different!

3115
02:35:44,380 --> 02:35:46,180
Wait, something's going in reverse!

3116
02:35:46,180 --> 02:35:52,760
What? What's going on?

3117
02:35:52,760 --> 02:35:55,760
There was nothing past Polka's end, right?

3118
02:35:55,760 --> 02:35:58,480
The goal!

3119
02:35:58,480 --> 02:36:00,360
The color? Did I get the color wrong?

3120
02:36:00,360 --> 02:36:03,360
Oh wait, I hadn't thought about colors at all!

3121
02:36:04,160 --> 02:36:06,160
Polka's colors are light blue and blue, right?

3122
02:36:06,160 --> 02:36:06,900
Yeah.

3123
02:36:06,900 --> 02:36:09,960
So that was actually the right answer.

3124
02:36:09,960 --> 02:36:11,960
Is this your first time on this stage?

3125
02:36:11,960 --> 02:36:14,900
With light blue and blue.

3126
02:36:14,900 --> 02:36:17,560
If we go light blue, it'll stop partway through.

3127
02:36:17,560 --> 02:36:19,560
So going as two is definitely the right call.

3128
02:36:19,560 --> 02:36:21,560
That part's where Unatán builds, right?

3129
02:36:21,560 --> 02:36:23,360
Oh, I see.

3130
02:36:23,360 --> 02:36:25,360
Even though Polpol was the one who went first.

3131
02:36:25,360 --> 02:36:27,160
You know this well.

3132
02:36:30,960 --> 02:36:33,760
And then Unatán builds the path.

3133
02:36:33,760 --> 02:36:34,760
Nice, nice!

3134
02:36:34,760 --> 02:36:36,560
Build it like this.

3135
02:36:36,560 --> 02:36:43,370
After this, if you can't press that button, the floor...

3136
02:36:43,370 --> 02:36:46,170
Won't open?

3137
02:36:46,170 --> 02:36:49,970
And since Unatán is pressing against the wall,

3138
02:36:49,970 --> 02:36:52,970
Ponpon can get through that hole,

3139
02:36:52,970 --> 02:36:55,770
but what do we do after that?

3140
02:36:55,770 --> 02:36:57,770
That's the problem — what comes after.

3141
02:36:58,570 --> 02:37:05,170
What was that about "the other way" earlier?

3142
02:37:05,170 --> 02:37:10,970
From here~

3143
02:37:10,970 --> 02:37:14,770
What are we supposed to do?

3144
02:37:14,770 --> 02:37:19,570
Is there nothing? Ponpon, go check below.

3145
02:37:19,570 --> 02:37:22,570
Aren't you scared? What if you disappear again?

3146
02:37:22,570 --> 02:37:27,370
It's fine, Uratán is holding the switch.

3147
02:37:27,370 --> 02:37:31,770
Connect with purple? Is that right?

3148
02:37:31,770 --> 02:37:37,050
Won't that close everything?

3149
02:37:37,050 --> 02:37:38,900
Oh! We made it!

3150
02:37:38,900 --> 02:37:43,700
Oh, there was a white wall over there! That's what it was!

3151
02:37:43,700 --> 02:37:49,620
Ahh, I'm floating~ floating~ floating~

3152
02:37:49,620 --> 02:37:52,050
We made it. Down, down. Okay!

3153
02:37:52,050 --> 02:37:56,050
We made it! I see — this stage is going to be a tough one.

3154
02:37:56,050 --> 02:38:00,880
Wait, this is just going to go on forever. Can't move. Yeah, this is hard. Can't control the inside.

3155
02:38:00,880 --> 02:38:05,850
Heave-ho, we made it! This is going to be quite the ordeal.

3156
02:38:05,850 --> 02:38:08,850
This time it's this ring.

3157
02:38:08,850 --> 02:38:14,450
I see, I see.

3158
02:38:17,690 --> 02:38:20,550
Got it~

3159
02:38:20,550 --> 02:38:27,790
I feel like my brain is getting smarter somehow, but it's really... my brain, like...

3160
02:38:27,790 --> 02:38:32,550
My brain is getting so tired. We're doing something incredible here.

3161
02:38:32,550 --> 02:38:39,950
Yeah, it really feels like studying — I can feel it in my brain. It's intense.

3162
02:38:39,950 --> 02:38:43,290
You feel like you're studying too, right?

3163
02:38:43,290 --> 02:38:47,470
Seriously... it's like physics or something.

3164
02:38:47,470 --> 02:38:49,170
It uses so much brainpower!

3165
02:38:49,170 --> 02:38:51,430
Like, my brain is seriously going crazy.

3166
02:38:51,430 --> 02:38:52,890
Let's just try jumping.

3167
02:38:52,890 --> 02:38:55,310
This is making me want to fall asleep.

3168
02:38:55,310 --> 02:38:58,670
How can you fall asleep in this state?

3169
02:38:58,670 --> 02:39:00,650
Anyway, I jumped and sank.

3170
02:39:00,650 --> 02:39:02,710
I want to fall asleep.

3171
02:39:02,710 --> 02:39:05,850
Okay, so let me try pressing something.

3172
02:39:05,850 --> 02:39:07,870
What happens if I press this?

3173
02:39:08,930 --> 02:39:10,950
Open up~

3174
02:39:10,950 --> 02:39:15,110
Galileo, Galileo~

3175
02:39:15,110 --> 02:39:17,870
Galileo, Galileo~

3176
02:39:17,870 --> 02:39:18,730
So it opens.

3177
02:39:18,730 --> 02:39:26,370
There's a warp zone over there.

3178
02:39:26,370 --> 02:39:28,230
Where does it go?

3179
02:39:28,230 --> 02:39:33,380
There's a launcher spot here.

3180
02:39:33,380 --> 02:39:34,680
Yeah, there's a launcher spot.

3181
02:39:34,680 --> 02:39:37,080
Looks like there might be a place to enter inside.

3182
02:39:37,080 --> 02:39:42,340
So to get Ponpon in there,

3183
02:39:42,340 --> 02:39:43,680
how do we get there?

3184
02:39:43,680 --> 02:39:48,270
If we connect that,

3185
02:39:48,270 --> 02:39:49,820
that should do it.

3186
02:39:49,820 --> 02:39:52,860
Does it disappear when Unatán goes there?

3187
02:39:52,860 --> 02:39:53,900
How do we connect it?

3188
02:39:53,900 --> 02:39:56,520
Wait, what are we connecting to what?

3189
02:39:56,520 --> 02:40:01,760
Let's try jumping from here.

3190
02:40:01,760 --> 02:40:03,360
Oh, no good.

3191
02:40:03,360 --> 02:40:07,060
Even if I jump, I can't reach the panel.

3192
02:40:07,060 --> 02:40:09,900
Huh? Where does this send you?

3193
02:40:09,900 --> 02:40:12,560
It's going somewhere that's not the panel.

3194
02:40:12,560 --> 02:40:15,560
The distance — what's with this awkward distance?

3195
02:40:15,560 --> 02:40:16,560
No, no.

3196
02:40:16,560 --> 02:40:19,310
Oh wait, can't we go in here?

3197
02:40:19,310 --> 02:40:21,160
So what?

3198
02:40:21,160 --> 02:40:22,960
"So what," she says.

3199
02:40:22,960 --> 02:40:25,960
You said "so what" today.

3200
02:40:25,960 --> 02:40:29,770
We'll definitely need that later.

3201
02:40:29,770 --> 02:40:32,370
If you press it like this,

3202
02:40:32,370 --> 02:40:35,540
that part gets opened.

3203
02:40:35,540 --> 02:40:39,410
So what does that mean?

3204
02:40:39,410 --> 02:40:42,140
With this...

3205
02:40:42,140 --> 02:40:44,940
Okay, like this...

3206
02:40:44,940 --> 02:40:46,740
A little higher?

3207
02:40:46,740 --> 02:40:49,340
Around here? Like this, like this, like this.

3208
02:40:49,340 --> 02:40:52,140
Push it a little more.

3209
02:40:52,140 --> 02:40:54,140
Yes! Got it, got it, got it!

3210
02:40:54,140 --> 02:40:58,140
Oh, somewhere was predicted, but it's definitely not there.

3211
02:40:58,140 --> 02:40:59,940
It's not the opposite either.

3212
02:40:59,940 --> 02:41:02,940
Uh, wh-wh-wh-what, something a little more...

3213
02:41:02,940 --> 02:41:05,740
Ah, ah, this, ah, something on the right side...

3214
02:41:05,740 --> 02:41:07,740
Can do it, can we do it?

3215
02:41:07,740 --> 02:41:08,740
Wobbly wobbly wobbly...

