03:23:07,280 --> 03:23:10,280
It might be better for Popo to hold it

4002
03:23:10,280 --> 03:23:12,080
Maybe so

4003
03:23:12,080 --> 03:23:17,530
How did you get in there while holding that?

4004
03:23:17,530 --> 03:23:18,510
This?

4005
03:23:18,510 --> 03:23:19,330
Jump

4006
03:23:19,330 --> 03:23:21,280
See!

4007
03:23:27,570 --> 03:23:31,530
Oh! Here we go, here we go! Hello!

4008
03:23:31,530 --> 03:23:33,470
Hm?

4009
03:23:33,470 --> 03:23:35,470
Oh, I pushed it—

4010
03:23:35,470 --> 03:23:37,070
Yes!

4011
03:23:37,070 --> 03:23:38,070
I pushed it!

4012
03:23:38,070 --> 03:23:42,050
That worked! Yay!

4013
03:23:42,050 --> 03:23:43,870
Ah, I see

4014
03:23:43,870 --> 03:23:45,670
Thank goodness

4015
03:23:45,670 --> 03:23:55,470
Yeah, you really need two people for this

4016
03:23:55,470 --> 03:23:59,070
Of course, you gotta combine your strength~

4017
03:23:59,070 --> 03:23:59,170
Of course, you gotta combine your strength~

4018
03:23:59,170 --> 03:24:00,970
Of course, you gotta combine your strength~ That's exactly it~

4019
03:24:00,970 --> 03:24:02,960
Phew~

4020
03:24:02,960 --> 03:24:04,570
Whew, congrats

4021
03:24:04,570 --> 03:24:06,500
That really took some brainpower

4022
03:24:06,500 --> 03:24:08,370
Yeah, no kidding

4023
03:24:08,370 --> 03:24:10,370
Going against the current was effective

4024
03:24:10,370 --> 03:24:12,370
But like, that warp thing—

4025
03:24:12,370 --> 03:24:14,370
The effect looks pretty though

4026
03:24:14,370 --> 03:24:16,170
True

4027
03:24:16,170 --> 03:24:18,170
Oh, there it is again

4028
03:24:18,170 --> 03:24:20,170
What is this

4029
03:24:20,170 --> 03:24:21,970
It looks pretty though

4030
03:24:21,970 --> 03:24:23,970
What is this thing

4031
03:24:23,970 --> 03:24:24,970
Whoa

4032
03:24:24,970 --> 03:24:25,970
You can't pass through here

4033
03:24:25,970 --> 03:24:28,770
First of all, what is this

4034
03:24:28,770 --> 03:24:30,570
Do we go in from here?

4035
03:24:30,570 --> 03:24:34,960
Well, it's above the warp

4036
03:24:34,960 --> 03:24:36,760
But wait, we'd get swept away—

4037
03:24:36,760 --> 03:24:38,760
The person being warped is—

4038
03:24:38,760 --> 03:24:42,760
Feels like it might connect somewhere

4039
03:24:42,760 --> 03:24:45,560
Where should I go?

4040
03:24:45,560 --> 03:24:48,360
Where should I go?

4041
03:24:48,360 --> 03:24:50,160
Tough call

4042
03:24:50,160 --> 03:24:53,060
But there's only here — where's next?

4043
03:24:53,060 --> 03:24:53,860
Oh, I can make it!

4044
03:24:53,860 --> 03:24:55,860
Ow! What?!

4045
03:24:55,860 --> 03:24:58,660
Something got in my way!

4046
03:24:58,660 --> 03:25:00,460
What? What just happened?

4047
03:25:00,460 --> 03:25:02,370
Something hit my head

4048
03:25:02,370 --> 03:25:05,260
Oh wait, there's something like spikes

4049
03:25:05,260 --> 03:25:07,060
So what are we supposed to do?

4050
03:25:07,060 --> 03:25:09,860
So there's something that stops those?

4051
03:25:09,860 --> 03:25:11,660
Can you crouch? Can you crouch here?

4052
03:25:11,660 --> 03:25:16,550
Would crouching work?

4053
03:25:16,550 --> 03:25:18,350
There's something there

4054
03:25:18,350 --> 03:25:21,910
Wait, this isn't like a pressure plate, is it?

4055
03:25:21,910 --> 03:25:24,210
It is!

4056
03:25:24,210 --> 03:25:26,630
It's coming from above! Attacking from above!

4057
03:25:26,630 --> 03:25:27,790
It is!

4058
03:25:27,790 --> 03:25:30,590
It was a pressure plate type thing

4059
03:25:30,590 --> 03:25:33,490
Huh? So then what do we do?

4060
03:25:33,490 --> 03:25:35,290
So how do we get through?

4061
03:25:35,290 --> 03:25:39,950
Is there something somewhere to stop it?

4062
03:25:39,950 --> 03:25:42,780
But wait, can't we just go through?

4063
03:25:44,430 --> 03:25:46,430
Try placing it there, Himemori

4064
03:25:46,430 --> 03:25:51,230
I think if you go through that thing here, you'll fall

4065
03:25:51,230 --> 03:25:53,230
You're right, yeah

4066
03:25:53,230 --> 03:25:57,030
Right, because there's a blue one — the barrier

4067
03:25:57,030 --> 03:26:00,830
Can we move sideways partway through?

4068
03:26:00,830 --> 03:26:11,580
What was that?

4069
03:26:11,580 --> 03:26:13,430
Where are you going, Polka?

4070
03:26:14,230 --> 03:26:16,050
Hold on

4071
03:26:16,050 --> 03:26:18,030
Is there something there?

4072
03:26:18,030 --> 03:26:19,830
This is no time to be talking

4073
03:26:19,830 --> 03:26:24,830
Ugh, it's set up so it just won't connect nicely

4074
03:26:24,830 --> 03:26:30,630
Past those blue dots, there seems to be something there

4075
03:26:30,630 --> 03:26:34,430
Those blue dots are actually supposed to be invisible

4076
03:26:34,430 --> 03:26:36,060
What was there earlier?

4077
03:26:36,060 --> 03:26:38,030
Oh, you can go this way!

4078
03:26:38,030 --> 03:26:43,330
Earlier it felt like you could extend it this way from here

4079
03:26:43,330 --> 03:26:50,690
Huh? So that means—?

4080
03:26:50,690 --> 03:27:00,150
Alright, let's go check it out

4081
03:27:00,150 --> 03:27:05,350
Oh sorry, Polka was making this over here and then Polka went over there too

4082
03:27:05,650 --> 03:27:07,710
Sorry, sorry, sorry, sorry! Heregori-san, please go ahead!

4083
03:27:07,710 --> 03:27:09,150
Go check it out for me!

4084
03:27:09,150 --> 03:27:11,290
Can you go take a look?

4085
03:27:11,290 --> 03:27:15,890
Sure! There were interesting things on both the right and left

4086
03:27:15,890 --> 03:27:18,910
Get back before you get crushed! Come back!

4087
03:27:18,910 --> 03:27:22,050
It's a hellish one-way path... can't go right anymore?

4088
03:27:22,050 --> 03:27:23,750
Here we go!

4089
03:27:23,750 --> 03:27:24,650
Hmm— ah! Ah!

4090
03:27:24,650 --> 03:27:26,950
Oh, we can go! We can make it!

4091
03:27:26,950 --> 03:27:31,020
Nice, we can do it!

4092
03:27:31,020 --> 03:27:32,360
U-chan, where is this?

4093
03:27:32,360 --> 03:27:34,360
Oh! Oh! I see, I see, I see, I see!

4094
03:27:34,360 --> 03:27:35,500
That's what I wanted to do

4095
03:27:35,500 --> 03:27:37,420
I can't tell the distance though

4096
03:27:37,420 --> 03:27:40,020
If you leave it like that it'll just go up

4097
03:27:40,020 --> 03:27:42,020
Oh, so I need to go up?

4098
03:27:42,020 --> 03:27:43,020
Like this?

4099
03:27:43,020 --> 03:27:43,820
Oh, how'd that go?

4100
03:27:43,820 --> 03:27:44,820
Oh, it's going, it's going!

4101
03:27:44,820 --> 03:27:46,620
Wow, nice!

4102
03:27:46,620 --> 03:27:48,620
Oh, it's working, it's working!

4103
03:27:48,620 --> 03:27:51,420
We're moving forward

4104
03:27:51,420 --> 03:27:52,420
Exit on the right

4105
03:27:52,420 --> 03:27:55,410
Something on the left

4106
03:27:55,410 --> 03:27:56,220
A switch?

4107
03:27:56,220 --> 03:27:57,820
A button?

4108
03:27:57,820 --> 03:27:59,820
Ooh, I'll press whatever it is

4109
03:27:59,820 --> 03:28:02,620
Hm? It reversed?

4110
03:28:03,620 --> 03:28:07,620
Oh, there's a button that reverses it

4111
03:28:07,620 --> 03:28:11,850
Why would you want to reverse it?

4112
03:28:11,850 --> 03:28:18,450
Because you have to break the spike gimmick

4113
03:28:18,450 --> 03:28:29,980
So is this the Popo version with Unatan right now?

4114
03:28:31,650 --> 03:28:35,140
Popo can get through — oh no, it's guarded

4115
03:28:35,140 --> 03:28:37,880
It's blocked by glass, can't get through

4116
03:28:37,880 --> 03:28:43,400
But if that disappears, then in the end...

4117
03:28:43,400 --> 03:28:46,360
Huh? Ahh...

4118
03:28:46,360 --> 03:28:48,780
Is that how it works?

4119
03:28:48,780 --> 03:28:53,420
I thought we could do it the same way as before

4120
03:28:53,420 --> 03:28:58,190
But if it's Popo-Popo, that part disappears, right?

4121
03:28:58,190 --> 03:29:04,080
Umm, ahhh, but wait — if Ponpon goes here...

4122
03:29:04,080 --> 03:29:08,980
The one above gets cut off, right? It disappears, doesn't it?

4123
03:29:08,980 --> 03:29:14,070
Hmm, what are we supposed to do?

4124
03:29:14,070 --> 03:29:16,750
Wait

4125
03:29:16,750 --> 03:29:19,330
Wai— ah!

4126
03:29:19,330 --> 03:29:24,530
Wait— can't wait— no, that's wrong

4127
03:29:24,530 --> 03:29:28,010
I can't help laughing — where do I need to connect this?

4128
03:29:28,370 --> 03:29:32,220
I want to connect Popo

4129
03:29:32,220 --> 03:29:37,480
The wall on this side is the ceiling and here

4130
03:29:37,480 --> 03:29:42,220
And here, but if it's here, Popo dies, right?

4131
03:29:42,220 --> 03:29:46,940
How do you do this?

4132
03:29:46,940 --> 03:29:47,460
Reverse

4133
03:29:47,460 --> 03:29:50,440
I think the reverse one is used somehow too

4134
03:29:50,440 --> 03:29:51,920
But how do you use it?

4135
03:29:57,460 --> 03:30:00,100
Was there anything on this side?

4136
03:30:00,100 --> 03:30:02,280
Was there nothing?

4137
03:30:02,280 --> 03:30:04,100
There's nothing...

4138
03:30:04,100 --> 03:30:07,100
Nothing below either

4139
03:30:07,100 --> 03:30:10,160
Top and bottom are flipped?

4140
03:30:10,160 --> 03:30:12,800
Where are the top and bottom?

4141
03:30:12,800 --> 03:30:15,260
Should Popo make something too?

4142
03:30:15,260 --> 03:30:16,140
Top and left

4143
03:30:16,140 --> 03:30:17,540
This side and...

4144
03:30:17,540 --> 03:30:19,100
Ahh, but... no, that won't work

4145
03:30:19,100 --> 03:30:21,380
Can Popo only flow through here?

4146
03:30:21,380 --> 03:30:22,640
Where is it? The reverse

4147
03:30:22,640 --> 03:30:23,900
Whoa!

4148
03:30:23,900 --> 03:30:27,800
A portal on the spike ceiling side

4149
03:30:27,800 --> 03:30:30,210
Ah!

4150
03:30:30,210 --> 03:30:31,750
Wait a moment

4151
03:30:31,750 --> 03:30:32,420
A flash of inspiration?

4152
03:30:32,420 --> 03:30:32,910
Hold on

4153
03:30:32,910 --> 03:30:33,910
A flash of inspiration?

4154
03:30:33,910 --> 03:30:36,710
Did an idea come? An idea!

4155
03:30:36,710 --> 03:30:40,480
An idea?

4156
03:30:40,480 --> 03:30:41,380
No wait

4157
03:30:41,380 --> 03:30:45,080
In that case...

4158
03:30:45,080 --> 03:30:46,980
Reverse it the moment it appears?

4159
03:30:46,980 --> 03:30:47,980
Like this

4160
03:30:47,980 --> 03:30:48,610
No, that's not it

4161
03:30:48,610 --> 03:30:51,660
Should I go down for now?

4162
03:30:51,660 --> 03:30:52,400
Ah, no that's wrong.

4163
03:30:52,400 --> 03:30:57,080
This is a na-portal, this is.

4164
03:30:57,080 --> 03:30:58,760
It's doing a na-portal, na—

4165
03:30:58,760 --> 03:31:02,640
Huh?

4166
03:31:02,640 --> 03:31:03,920
W-wait, I'm getting confused.

4167
03:31:03,920 --> 03:31:05,020
Hmm? Hmm, what's going on?

4168
03:31:05,020 --> 03:31:05,660
W-wait.

4169
03:31:05,660 --> 03:31:06,610
Oh, oh!

4170
03:31:06,610 --> 03:31:09,260
So close but can't make it, so close but can't make it!

4171
03:31:09,260 --> 03:31:10,160
This is so frustrating.

4172
03:31:10,160 --> 03:31:10,760
W-what's going on?

4173
03:31:10,760 --> 03:31:12,000
It's so hard and frustrating.

4174
03:31:12,000 --> 03:31:13,360
Huh, wait.

4175
03:31:13,360 --> 03:31:14,240
Hmm? Hmm?

4176
03:31:14,240 --> 03:31:16,080
I can't move carelessly, and this side too...

4177
03:31:16,080 --> 03:31:18,760
For now, po—

4178
03:31:18,760 --> 03:31:19,360
Ah, wait.

4179
03:31:19,360 --> 03:31:23,060
No, hold on. I want to move the po-po from here to over there!

4180
03:31:23,060 --> 03:31:24,020
Okay, okay.

4181
03:31:24,020 --> 03:31:27,500
If the po-po goes to the ceiling and the starting point...

4182
03:31:27,500 --> 03:31:30,950
But wait...

4183
03:31:30,950 --> 03:31:35,950
If the po-po goes to the ceiling and the starting point, the moment po-po enters, the ceiling one gets cut off.

4184
03:31:35,950 --> 03:31:38,610
Right, it disappears here.

4185
03:31:38,610 --> 03:31:40,910
So if I want to reverse it...

4186
03:31:40,910 --> 03:31:46,410
I thought about making it after passing through, but would that even work?

4187
03:31:48,160 --> 03:31:53,360
If I draw it after passing through, there's a chance it works.

4188
03:31:53,360 --> 03:31:56,360
This reverse run...

4189
03:31:56,360 --> 03:31:58,980
Reverse...

4190
03:31:58,980 --> 03:32:06,030
No wait, po—

4191
03:32:06,030 --> 03:32:12,590
—tan is...

4192
03:32:12,590 --> 03:32:18,070
Here and here.

4193
03:32:18,070 --> 03:32:20,190
What about this?

4194
03:32:20,190 --> 03:32:24,120
Hmm, if it's this way I can get through~

4195
03:32:24,120 --> 03:32:26,920
But if I do this, I'll get guillotined.

4196
03:32:26,920 --> 03:32:30,720
So I drop off partway, like Luna did earlier.

4197
03:32:30,720 --> 03:32:31,520
Oh!

4198
03:32:31,520 --> 03:32:32,520
Let me try it!

4199
03:32:32,520 --> 03:32:36,320
Okay. Can I drop down like before?

4200
03:32:36,320 --> 03:32:39,320
Can I fall to the middle with this?

4201
03:32:39,320 --> 03:32:42,120
WAAAAAAH! Dangerous dangerous dangerous!

4202
03:32:42,120 --> 03:32:43,720
That was close!

4203
03:32:43,720 --> 03:32:47,720
Huh? Oh, it's not moving. Nobody's carrying it anymore.

4204
03:32:47,720 --> 03:32:51,920
Did it go to the middle? It did!

4205
03:32:51,920 --> 03:32:54,520
If it went to the middle, then with this—

4206
03:32:54,520 --> 03:32:57,520
The po-po gets carried straight up and—

4207
03:32:57,520 --> 03:33:03,320
Can it come this way? Oh it came, it came, it came!

4208
03:33:03,320 --> 03:33:12,920
So that's how it works! You make the entrance by running it in reverse!

4209
03:33:12,920 --> 03:33:16,920
You make it with po-po and the una-tan reverses.

4210
03:33:16,920 --> 03:33:18,920
Whoooa!

4211
03:33:18,920 --> 03:33:19,920
I see, I see.

4212
03:33:19,920 --> 03:33:21,920
So that was the reverse-run button.

4213
03:33:21,920 --> 03:33:23,920
It's not the one where you press the square, I think.

4214
03:33:23,920 --> 03:33:25,920
Reverse run, reverse run.

4215
03:33:25,920 --> 03:33:29,920
The reversal makes total sense now.

4216
03:33:29,920 --> 03:33:32,720
I was totally relying on the na-portal.

4217
03:33:32,720 --> 03:33:34,720
Thank youuu~

4218
03:33:34,720 --> 03:33:35,520
I did it!

4219
03:33:35,520 --> 03:33:39,360
Una-tan hasn't done anything useful at all either.

4220
03:33:39,360 --> 03:33:42,520
This is crazy, this whole "transport" thing—

4221
03:33:42,520 --> 03:33:45,520
It's way too much. Seriously insane.

4222
03:33:45,520 --> 03:33:48,900
My brain is running at full capacity like never before.

4223
03:33:48,900 --> 03:33:49,900
Anyway, I'll jump!

4224
03:33:49,900 --> 03:33:52,040
Gooooo dooooown~

4225
03:33:52,040 --> 03:33:53,200
Ah, I see.

4226
03:33:53,200 --> 03:33:56,000
So it's just a matter of going to the other side.

4227
03:33:56,000 --> 03:33:58,000
There's some kind of board here.

4228
03:33:58,360 --> 03:34:00,360
Oh, it's over there.

4229
03:34:00,360 --> 03:34:04,700
What's this?

4230
03:34:04,700 --> 03:34:06,920
So the funnel is over there.

4231
03:34:06,920 --> 03:34:08,920
Then I can go here, at least.

4232
03:34:08,920 --> 03:34:14,180
Is this another reverse flow? Yeah, reverse flow.

4233
03:34:14,180 --> 03:34:18,370
This is about all I can use.

4234
03:34:18,370 --> 03:34:20,910
How do I get it into that side?

4235
03:34:20,910 --> 03:34:22,710
I can get it in, I can get it in.

4236
03:34:22,710 --> 03:34:25,230
Oh, isn't this it?

4237
03:34:25,230 --> 03:34:27,230
But then the question is how to get to the middle.

4238
03:34:27,690 --> 03:34:30,490
Aiyah~

4239
03:34:30,490 --> 03:34:32,290
It came that way though.

4240
03:34:32,290 --> 03:34:36,290
From here, I can only push it about this far.

4241
03:34:36,290 --> 03:34:40,090
But from here,

4242
03:34:40,090 --> 03:34:44,340
I can't get out from there.

4243
03:34:44,340 --> 03:34:46,140
So we send out those two?

4244
03:34:46,140 --> 03:34:48,140
It's about sending out those two,

4245
03:34:48,140 --> 03:34:50,140
but then what? You know?

4246
03:34:50,140 --> 03:34:55,980
How? In that case, Uratan goes like this and—

4247
03:34:55,980 --> 03:34:58,400
connects this place and that place.

4248
03:34:58,400 --> 03:34:59,310
But yeah, that's the thing.

4249
03:34:59,310 --> 03:35:00,520
Doesn't it feel like, "wait, what?"

4250
03:35:00,520 --> 03:35:05,200
How about going this way here?

4251
03:35:05,200 --> 03:35:06,240
Oh, it's blocked.

4252
03:35:06,240 --> 03:35:09,480
Where's the white wall?

4253
03:35:09,480 --> 03:35:12,060
There isn't one...

4254
03:35:12,060 --> 03:35:12,760
First, the middle.

4255
03:35:12,760 --> 03:35:13,900
Oh, what's this?

4256
03:35:13,900 --> 03:35:15,600
Oh, can I jump in this state?

4257
03:35:15,600 --> 03:35:18,110
Oh!

4258
03:35:18,110 --> 03:35:19,230
Whoa!

4259
03:35:19,230 --> 03:35:20,510
Oh, but I fell.

4260
03:35:20,510 --> 03:35:22,350
Well, I managed to fall at least.

4261
03:35:22,350 --> 03:35:25,500
Oh, there's a barrier above.

4262
03:35:25,500 --> 03:35:27,940
So I go here?

4263
03:35:27,940 --> 03:35:33,310
Then do I flow through again like just now? Shoot downward?

4264
03:35:33,310 --> 03:35:39,860
If I shoot down— oh, I see, nice nice nice!

4265
03:35:39,860 --> 03:35:44,780
With this, there's a barrier here and I'll fall.

4266
03:35:44,780 --> 03:35:47,150
So that's the kind of thing Polka would make!

